 (see manual for references)

 Bader atomic properties are calculated using a grid-based method
 reported in the articles
 - Juan I. Rodriguez et al. J. Comput. Chem. 30 (2009) 1082.
 - Juan I. Rodriguez, R.F.W. Bader, P.W. Ayers, C. Michel, A.W. Gotz, C. Bo,
   Chem. Phys. Lett. 472 (2009) 149.
 The convergence of the atomic integration of the Laplacian is
 not monotone but sinusoidal. So the integration of the Laplacian
 is not always closer to zero as a larger grid is used
 (see references above).


